<title>JAPAN: Japan Dec cocoa bean imports up 77.7 pct yr/yr-MOF.</title>
<headline>Japan Dec cocoa bean imports up 77.7 pct yr/yr-MOF.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's cocoa bean imports in December totalled 1,697 tonnes, up 77.7 percent from the same month a year earlier, according to Ministry of Finance data released on Monday. The following is a breakdown (in tonnes):</p>
<p>			Dec 96	  Nov 96	 Dec 95</p>
<p> Total		1,697	   1,542	    955</p>
<p>Major suppliers (in tonnes):</p>
<p> Ghana		  nil	     599	    276</p>
<p> Venezuela	     49		25	     38</p>
<p> Ecuador		570	     350	    475</p>
<p>Cumulative cocoa bean imports in calendar 1996 were 49,649 tonnes, up 21.2 percent from 40,996 tonnes a year earlier. Imports of other cocoa products were as follows (in tonnes):</p>
<p>			 Dec 96	 Nov 96	  Dec 95</p>
<p> Cocoa paste	  254	     145	     174</p>
<p> Defatted paste	36	     180	     nil</p>
<p> Cocoa butter     1,429	   1,003	  12,898</p>
<p> Cocoa powder     1,044	   1,113	   6,309</p>
<p>Chocolate</p>
<p>   confectionery  1,983	   2,322	   2,287</p>
<p>--Tokyo Commodity Desk +81-3-3432-6179</p>
</text>
